# Build output
bin/
bin/Debug/
bin/Dev/
bin/Release/
bin/Sanitize/
bin/Coverage/
bin/Profile/
bin/TSan/
make/

# Fuzzing output.  The seed corpus under test/fuzz/corpus/ is tracked on
# purpose — it is the regression corpus and is regenerated by
# test/fuzz/make_corpus.py — but crash reproducers and the clang/libFuzzer
# binaries are per-run and are not.
#
# bin/fuzz-corpus/ is the *working* corpus: the directory libFuzzer writes its
# discoveries into, and the one CI carries between runs through actions/cache.
# It is deliberately not tracked.  It used to be the seed directory, and a few
# nights of that put 7158 unreadable files into the repository — see the note at
# the top of test/fuzz/run_fuzz.sh.
bin/fuzz-artifacts/
bin/fuzz-corpus/
bin/fuzz-libfuzzer/

# The same directory, unanchored, because the replay driver writes its crash
# artifact relative to the working directory rather than to bin/.  Running a
# target by hand from the repository root — which is how anyone reproduces a
# failure — therefore drops fuzz-artifacts/ here instead, where the anchored
# rule above does not reach it.  Found by doing exactly that.
fuzz-artifacts/

# Load harness and suite logs
suite-*.log
load-*.log
release-build.log

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Benchmark results
test/benchmark/results/

# Compiled benchmark helpers.  Both were tracked as prebuilt ELF binaries beside
# their own sources, since the initial commit -- so the repository shipped
# executables built on one machine against that machine's libc, and
# bench_generator.sh exec'd one of them rather than building it.  Each .c file
# has carried its own compile line in its header comment the whole time.
test/benchmark/bench_cache_vs_redis
test/benchmark/bench_client

# Packages
*.deb
*.rpm
# every .md is local unless it is named below.
# ai-assist notes, handoffs and memory dumps are markdown and kept arriving;
# ignoring the extension and listing the public docs errs closed instead.
# already-tracked files stay tracked -- the negations are what keeps them
# obvious rather than what keeps them working.
*.md
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!examples/**/README.md
!man/README.md
!.github/**/*.md

# IDE and editor
.vscode/
.idea/
.vs/
.DS_Store

# gcov writes these beside the objects (make/ is ignored) and .gcov files into
# whatever directory it is run from, which is not always make/.
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.gcov

# Agent scratch, none of it project configuration.  `.claude/worktrees/` holds
# live git worktrees -- 2.1 GiB of them at the time of writing -- the lock file
# belongs to whatever is running, and RESUME.md is one session's state.
#
# The whole directory rather than a list of its parts: two separate rules used
# to cover worktrees/ and the lock file while disagreeing in their comments
# about whether the rest was trackable, and RESUME.md fell through the gap
# between them.  Erring closed means anything here that the project genuinely
# wants to share has to be added with an explicit `git add -f`, which is the
# deliberate decision the old comment asked for and did not enforce.
.claude/

# Built by scripts/build-thirdparty.sh http3, headers and archives alike.
/thirdparty/openssl/
/thirdparty/ngtcp2/
/thirdparty/nghttp3/

# scripts/update.sh: which pins of scripts/build-thirdparty.sh the archives here were built from
thirdparty/.built-versions
thirdparty/premake/

# What building the Rust binding leaves behind.
sdk/rust/Cargo.lock
sdk/rust/target/
sdk/node/build/
